    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 4. Weak picks + leakage check\n",
        "\n",
        "**Weak picks (to fill in from the real top-20 table above):** identify the 1-3 rows in the top\n",
        "20 with the smallest `ctr_gap` magnitude or borderline `content_age_days_march` — these are the\n",
        "ones riding mostly on one signal rather than both, and are the first I'd drop if reviewer\n",
        "capacity (Week 1: ~50/week) got tighter.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Leakage check:** confirmed below in code — the rule's inputs are exactly\n",
        "`content_age_days_march` and `ctr_gap` (itself built only from `avg_position_march` and\n",
        "`ctr_march`), all fully knowable by end of March. `clicks_april` and `is_declining_april` never\n",
        "appear on the right-hand side of the score formula."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Mh7-3LY5kScI"
      },
      "id": "Mh7-3LY5kScI"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "rule_input_cols = {'content_age_days_march', 'avg_position_march', 'ctr_march', 'ctr_gap'}\n",
        "forbidden_cols = {'clicks_april', 'is_declining_april'}\n",
        "\n",
        "# The exact expression used to build rule_score, re-stated for an explicit audit:\n",
        "score_formula_inputs = {'content_age_days_march', 'ctr_gap'}\n",
        "leak_found = score_formula_inputs & forbidden_cols\n",
        "print(f\"Columns used directly in rule_score: {score_formula_inputs}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Forbidden (label-derived / future-window) columns: {forbidden_cols}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Overlap (should be EMPTY): {leak_found}\")\n",
        "assert len(leak_found) == 0, \"LEAKAGE: a forbidden column was used as a rule input!\"\n",
        "print(\"\\nConfirmed: no future-window or label-derived inputs in the rule.\")"
